vine 1.2.0
prefix: game-surface
title: Make GameSurface the reusable agent-facing game surface
---
[root] Make GameSurface the reusable agent-facing game surface (complete)
Goal: A game can expose deterministic observation, journal authoring, and speculative branch work to an agent through one generic MCP surface.
Question: Which part of that surface belongs in the reusable engine, and which part remains game meaning supplied by the package?
Accept: The surface supports explicit-time observation, journal read/write, branch creation, preview, commit, comparison, and discard. Actual history remains independently recoverable after speculative work. A synthetic consumer and the voxel sample use the same MCP server.
-> camera
-> docs
> GameSurface owns the agent-facing capability boundary; it does not become a second domain model.
> The actual worldline remains immutable. MCP session state selects and names histories; it does not mutate published values in place.
> Branch writes use an expected revision and return a new revision. Actual-line writes are visibly distinct from speculative branch writes.
@guidance text/markdown proposals/library-contract.md
@guidance text/markdown proposals/rendering-contract.md
@file text/markdown evidence/pure-engine-experiment.md
@file text/markdown evidence/pure-engine-scaling.md
