[contract] Define the typed history and GameSurface contract (complete)
Files: crates/engine-surface/Cargo.toml; crates/engine-surface/src/lib.rs; crates/engine-api/Cargo.toml; crates/engine-api/src/lib.rs
Do: Add immutable branch-session handles, revisions, branch descriptors, JSON fact requests, preview/commit result values, and the GameSurface trait. Keep branch storage generic over context and fact payload; keep JSON/schema at the agent-facing boundary. Preserve actual history when branches are discarded.
Accept: Unit tests cover actual and counterfactual handles, fork-boundary protection, stale-revision rejection, preview immutability, commit replacement, and discard recovery. No voxel or Caravan types enter the contract.
---
[synthetic] Prove the surface with a generic typed consumer (complete)
Files: crates/engine-surface/tests/surface.rs; crates/engine-observation-mcp/src/lib.rs
Do: Implement a small synthetic surface over byte facts or color facts. Exercise manifest, journal read, branch open, JSON fact validation, preview, commit, metadata/snapshot, comparison inputs, and discard through the generic server types.
Accept: The synthetic surface proves branch work changes only the selected branch, the actual revision remains stable, stale writes fail, and the generic MCP server exposes the same tools used by voxel.
-> contract
